      "content": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "nf6psig",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Kingdom Monera"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "05h6f6w",
      "content": "Monera includes prokaryotic organisms like bacteria and cyanobacteria. They lack true nucleus and membrane-bound organelles."
    },
    {
      "id": "ao8p1ht",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Details</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cell Type</p>",
            "<p>Prokaryotic</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cell Wall</p>",
            "<p>Peptidoglycan</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Examples</p>",
            "<p>E. coli, Nostoc</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "z0vglg6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Kingdom Protista"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iqu8vjz",
      "content": "Protista includes unicellular eukaryotes like Amoeba and Paramecium. Some are photosynthetic (Euglena), others are parasitic (Plasmodium)."
    },
    {
      "id": "v5con02",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Kingdom Fungi"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dds1u43",
      "content": "Fungi are heterotrophic organisms with chitin cell wall. They obtain food by absorption and reproduce by spores."
    },
    {
      "id": "rb3fo2z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Kingdom Plantae"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4i0frk4",
      "content": "Plantae includes multicellular autotrophic organisms with cellulose cell wall and chlorophyll."
    },
    {
      "id": "v0w4uc2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Kingdom Animalia"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vsppvvh",
      "content": "Animalia includes multicellular heterotrophic organisms without cell wall. They show advanced body organization and organ systems."
    },
    {
      "id": "ijvx0lr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Hierarchical Levels of Classification"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8b1g6pw",
      "content": "Classification follows hierarchy: Kingdom → Phylum → Class → Order → Family → Genus → Species."
    },
    {
      "id": "9f6ml93",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. Binomial Nomenclature"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ww54t2d",
      "content": "Binomial nomenclature was introduced by Carolus Linnaeus. Each organism has two names: Genus and Species."
    },
